-- tests: the workspace suite as TWO SCOPE SHARDS, generated. Until 2026-10-02 this was one gate,
-- `test`, scope `**`, so its verdict could never be reused at another tree: every tree re-ran all
-- 8,538 tests. A shard's scope is DERIVED from cargo's dependency graph plus the fixtures its tests
-- were measured to read (scripts/gatehouse-test-shards.py, .gatehouse/test-shards.json), and the
-- lane MATERIALIZES it: the pod holds exactly the selected files, so a shard's verdict is a
-- function of its scope hash and a tree whose hash is unchanged may take the last held receipt
-- (verify_receipt's cross-tree branch: a kernel-DERIVED hash, the same hash, a materialized run).
--
-- WHY TWO. Measured on nucleus 2fc73eda over the 40 merged PRs before it (gatehouse
-- docs/sublinear-testing.md): the suite is 101.6 s of wall in a 3-CPU pod (303 s of test work),
-- and an attempt costs ~130-200 s more around it (prepare, ~20 s of hashing per step, the SDK
-- step, the pod's fixed start). A third shard costs more in attempts than it saves in tests.
--
--   test-node  nucleus-node's cluster (13 packages) and the four test binaries that read the whole
--              repository (nucleus-node::olog, xtask's own tests, nucleus-action-key's
--              escapes_population, nucleus-delivery-conformance's claim_honesty). Their scope is
--              `**` wherever they live; this is the shard that changes on most trees anyway. It
--              gets a git checkout (escapes_population runs `git ls-files`) and keeps no history.
--   test-libs  every other member, scope derived: `--workspace --exclude <test-node's>`, so a
--              crate added later is SELECTED at run time, and test-shard.py refuses to test it as
--              an empty stub until its directory is in this scope (the shadow found 66 tests of a
--              crate the first generation left out: no shard ran them, and both said held).
--
-- SAME BINARIES AS THE WHOLE-WORKSPACE RUN. `-p` alone unifies features over the selection, and
-- cargo then builds different test binaries from `cargo test --workspace` (382 of 1,568 units for
-- test-libs). scripts/test-shard.py --workspace-features turns on cargo's workspace feature
-- unification for the shard's process tree, and then 0 units differ (cargo's own unit graph,
-- compared unit by unit with every dependency). The flag is unstable in cargo 1.96.
--
-- measuredMs is an ESTIMATE from docker pods of the gate recipe (gatehouse shadow, 2026-10-02),
-- not the lane; the first lane runs are the measurement.
-- BEGIN generated by scripts/gatehouse-test-shards.py: edit .gatehouse/test-shards.json, not this block
let testNodeCap : ci.Cap = (tag 3 0, tag 3 1, 1800000, 1800000, 8192, [#b"**", #b"scripts/**"] : Bytes, [#b"target/**", #b"sdks/verifier-js/pkg/**", #b"sdks/verifier-js/target/**", #b"crates/*/src/lib.rs", #b"crates/*/src/main.rs", #b"crates/*/src/bin/*"] : Bytes, [] : Bytes)
